# ---- build / local scratch: never published -----------------------------------
# `.scratch/` holds text extracted from the original task papers and the raw data.
# Those are third-party materials, so they must not reach GitHub. The posts are
# written FROM this material, in the author's own words, but the material stays local.
.scratch/

# `tools/` holds the curation scripts, kept local on purpose: the branding guard and
# the rename table have to contain the board's name literally in order to match it, so
# publishing them would leak exactly what they exist to remove. They also hard-code
# absolute local paths, so they would be useless to a reader anyway.
tools/

# ---- source-collection junk (the sync script filters these, belt and braces) ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.vscode/
.continue/

# ---- data: a code repo should not carry it -------------------------------------
# (the sync script already refuses these; listed so a stray copy can never be staged)
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.db
*.npy
*.npz
*.pkl
*.model
*.docx
*.pptx

# ...but stopword lists ARE part of the code, so they are carved back in.
# Without these negations the blanket `*.csv` above would silently drop them.
!code/**/stop*.csv
!code/**/Stop*.csv

# ---- submission artifacts ------------------------------------------------------
*_results.csv
*[Aa]ns*.csv
~$*

# ---- logs / os ----
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
